     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"The target crown:obtain is an OR, so h3_0:obtain, h3_1:traverse and h3_2:obtain must all be made unreachable. Blocking h1_2:obtain cuts h3_0:obtain, since h1_2 is its only parent. It also cuts h3_2:obtain, which is an AND that needs h1_2. h3_1:traverse is still reachable through h2_0:traverse (from edge1:reach) and h2_2:access (via h1_1:traverse), so it must be blocked directly. One block cannot work: stopping h3_1 needs either h3_1 itself blocked or all three of its parents blocked, and blocking h3_1 alone leaves h3_0 and h3_2 reachable. So the minimum is 2: {h1_2:obtain, h3_1:traverse}.\"}"
    }
